# What `docker build` must never see when the repository root is the build context
# (backend/Dockerfile and feed/Dockerfile). The Dockerfiles copy only backend/, feed/,
# packages/clinsim and models/, but the whole context is still sent to the Docker daemon, and a
# careless `COPY . .` would bake these into an image. Keeping the secrets and the big folders
# out here is what makes "no key ever reaches an image" true, and it makes builds faster.
.git
.env
k8s/secret.env
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/.vite
feed/data
training
evals
docs
scratch
*.md
